# Vercel only builds the Vite frontend (see vercel.json: framework=vite,
# buildCommand=vite build, output=dist). Everything dynamic — /api/*, sitemaps,
# bot prerender, OG images — is proxied to the Railway backend via rewrites, so
# Vercel never needs these directories.
#
# Critically, Vercel's zero-config Serverless Functions feature auto-bundles any
# root-level `api/` directory as functions, regardless of framework. Those
# functions are dead here (the rewrites shadow them), and bundling api/server.js
# pulls heavy backend deps (googleapis, etc.) into a function that can exceed
# Vercel's size limit and fail the deploy. Excluding api/ stops that.
#
# NOTE: do NOT ignore scripts/ — npm's postinstall runs scripts/patch-apple-signin.sh
# during Vercel's install step.

api
supabase
ios
android
